{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T07:22:29.440Z","ordinal":82048,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0a4b20de840ea00d016ac35021057087d2a43483049a671f02","status":"completed","call_id":"call_Dyaiw362XD5Y1iVLJdbXaR3u","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md\\n@@\\n # Testcenter parity checklist\\n \\n+### Run-bound state, assets, links and live updates\\n+\\n+Original `TestController::get` addresses the selected test by its explicit ID;\\n+the Rewrite's current-state endpoint previously ignored a requested Run ID and\\n+returned the run with the latest `updatedAt`. Current-state and SSE now accept\\n+an optional `testRunId`, validate ownership against the authenticated session,\\n+tenant and workspace, and read that exact run. Unknown/foreign IDs return the\\n+same HTTP 404; an explicit empty ID fails rather than falling back. Reading a\\n+completed or monitor-paused run does not resume/reset it. A completed selected\\n+run cannot open a live stream for an unrelated running run.\\n+\\n+Participant state and asset-preload requests bind the selected ID. Live clients\\n+reconnect when the selected Run changes, reject another run's frames before\\n+acknowledging them, and ignore late headers from a replaced generation.\\n+Participant/monitor/detail re-entry links now carry the exact Run ID; participant\\n+links also preserve the preset assignment key. The URL, not another tab's\\n+persisted runtime, owns explicit re-entry selection. Historical session-only\\n+links and unselected API readers retain their chronological fallback. No schema,\\n+saved answer, lifecycle guard or participant credential was changed.\\n+\\n+The API regression fails before the change with the wrong Run ID; the preceding\\n+frontend fails the new real-link assertion. All 163 API tests pass in each of\\n+memory, File and SQLite, plus 165 core, 12 presence and 91 frontend tests. Real\\n+protected SQLite/browser flows pass in both interfaces with frozen production\\n+and development frontends, including actual generated links, hard reload,\\n+scoped live acknowledgement, monitor pause/resume and independent background\\n+answer saves. Production also passes headlessly. Its mandatory variant smoke\\n+seeds the second open Run through the owned repository: this proves selection\\n+isolation, not the still-blocked second starter launch. The preceding shared\\n+browser flow through completed session re-entry/clear and all 48 production\\n+starter states also pass. Production is 469.82kB under the unchanged 470kB limit.\\n+Evidence is retained in ignored `.data/run-selection-20261005.*`; PostgreSQL and\\n+complete publication CI remain independent proof.\\n+\\n ### Exact preset-variant re-entry\\n@@\\n-Both current-state readers also select a run by `updatedAt`, not by an explicit\\n-participant selection. Removing the conflict alone would let a later background\\n-answer save select an unrelated run. The fix must persist/authorize selection\\n-independently of response chronology and atomically reuse each assignment's run.\\n+The explicit run-bound selection prerequisite above is now implemented and\\n+tested independently of response chronology. Legacy session-only readers still\\n+use an `updatedAt` fallback. The launch conflict itself and atomic per-assignment\\n+run creation/reuse remain open; removing the conflict alone is not sufficient.\\n*** Update File: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md\\n@@\\n ## Acceptance matrix\\n \\n+Both interfaces now bind the selected Run ID through state, asset preload,\\n+live updates and actual generated re-entry links. Exact preset assignment,\\n+Unicode answers and Run ID survive hard reload; another run's later background\\n+saves cannot steal selection or bypass the selected run's monitor pause.\\n+Production/development protected SQLite browsers and headless production pass.\\n+The second open run in this focused fixture is repository-seeded, not started\\n+through the still-blocked P0 workflow. These shared functional safeguards do not\\n+close any full rendered-UI acceptance row or pixel-identity claim.\\n+\\n The shared backend now permits exact preset-assignment resumption after returning\\n@@\\n-also reproduced: another unfinished Booklet blocks an otherwise available\\n-selection, and current-state selection follows answer-update chronology. The\\n+also reproduced: another unfinished Booklet blocks an otherwise available\\n+selection. Explicit run-bound reads now avoid answer-update chronology, while\\n+historical session-only links retain that fallback. The\\n*** Update File: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/README.md\\n@@\\n fix does not yet permit switching to another unfinished Booklet; that separate\\n P0 and full Original-UI acceptance remain explicitly open in `docs/PARITY.md`.\\n+\\n+New session re-entry links include the exact Run ID and preset assignment.\\n+Both interfaces bind state, asset loading and live updates to that authorized\\n+Run, so another test's background saves cannot replace the selected test.\\n+Historical session-only links remain supported. The focused smoke also proves\\n+selection isolation and monitor pause/resume with an explicitly owned two-run\\n+repository fixture; it does not claim the second starter launch is implemented.\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cp /tmp/testcenter-run-selection-before-fix.log /tmp/testcenter-run-selection-browser-before-ui-fix.log /tmp/testcenter-run-selection-full-memory.log /tmp/testcenter-run-selection-full-file.log /tmp/testcenter-run-selection-full-sqlite.log /tmp/testcenter-run-selection-unit-tests.log /tmp/testcenter-run-selection-production-build.log /tmp/testcenter-run-selection-development-build.log /tmp/testcenter-run-selection-browser-production.log /tmp/testcenter-run-selection-browser-development.log /tmp/testcenter-run-selection-browser-ci.log /tmp/testcenter-run-selection-starter-production.log /tmp/testcenter-run-selection-session-link-regression.log .data/run-selection-20261005.G48v9l/; cp scripts/smoke-participant-booklet-variant.mjs scripts/participant-session-links.test.mjs scripts/event-stream-watchdog.test.mjs .data/run-selection-20261005.G48v9l/; cp -R /var/folders/0g/0jg2ynjn33sftyg101714qvw0000gn/T/testcenter-participant-variant-GT3Oea /var/folders/0g/0jg2ynjn33sftyg101714qvw0000gn/T/testcenter-participant-variant-AKfPCo /var/folders/0g/0jg2ynjn33sftyg101714qvw0000gn/T/testcenter-participant-variant-ehn4Y6 .data/run-selection-20261005.G48v9l/; git diff --check; shasum -a 256 docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx; git status --short\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",\"max_output_tokens\":1600}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10a80-143a-7c31-9fdf-94d993712507","create_time":1791184911.283948}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T07:22:29.461Z","ordinal":82049,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a10a80-143a-7c31-9fdf-94d993712507","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-63a87c6b-60f4-4ab0-92ac-c4077532dec9","changes":{"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/README.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -53,2 +53,9 @@\n \n+New session re-entry links include the exact Run ID and preset assignment.\n+Both interfaces bind state, asset loading and live updates to that authorized\n+Run, so another test's background saves cannot replace the selected test.\n+Historical session-only links remain supported. The focused smoke also proves\n+selection isolation and monitor pause/resume with an explicitly owned two-run\n+repository fixture; it does not claim the second starter launch is implemented.\n+\n The optional Systemcheck Unit surface uses the same sandboxed Verona host and\n","move_path":null},"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -2,2 +2,36 @@\n \n+### Run-bound state, assets, links and live updates\n+\n+Original `TestController::get` addresses the selected test by its explicit ID;\n+the Rewrite's current-state endpoint previously ignored a requested Run ID and\n+returned the run with the latest `updatedAt`. Current-state and SSE now accept\n+an optional `testRunId`, validate ownership against the authenticated session,\n+tenant and workspace, and read that exact run. Unknown/foreign IDs return the\n+same HTTP 404; an explicit empty ID fails rather than falling back. Reading a\n+completed or monitor-paused run does not resume/reset it. A completed selected\n+run cannot open a live stream for an unrelated running run.\n+\n+Participant state and asset-preload requests bind the selected ID. Live clients\n+reconnect when the selected Run changes, reject another run's frames before\n+acknowledging them, and ignore late headers from a replaced generation.\n+Participant/monitor/detail re-entry links now carry the exact Run ID; participant\n+links also preserve the preset assignment key. The URL, not another tab's\n+persisted runtime, owns explicit re-entry selection. Historical session-only\n+links and unselected API readers retain their chronological fallback. No schema,\n+saved answer, lifecycle guard or participant credential was changed.\n+\n+The API regression fails before the change with the wrong Run ID; the preceding\n+frontend fails the new real-link assertion. All 163 API tests pass in each of\n+memory, File and SQLite, plus 165 core, 12 presence and 91 frontend tests. Real\n+protected SQLite/browser flows pass in both interfaces with frozen production\n+and development frontends, including actual generated links, hard reload,\n+scoped live acknowledgement, monitor pause/resume and independent background\n+answer saves. Production also passes headlessly. Its mandatory variant smoke\n+seeds the second open Run through the owned repository: this proves selection\n+isolation, not the still-blocked second starter launch. The preceding shared\n+browser flow through completed session re-entry/clear and all 48 production\n+starter states also pass. Production is 469.82kB under the unchanged 470kB limit.\n+Evidence is retained in ignored `.data/run-selection-20261005.*`; PostgreSQL and\n+complete publication CI remain independent proof.\n+\n ### Exact preset-variant re-entry\n@@ -61,6 +95,6 @@\n first run returned to the starter. This is not completed multi-Booklet parity.\n-Both current-state readers also select a run by `updatedAt`, not by an explicit\n-participant selection. Removing the conflict alone would let a later background\n-answer save select an unrelated run. The fix must persist/authorize selection\n-independently of response chronology and atomically reuse each assignment's run.\n+The explicit run-bound selection prerequisite above is now implemented and\n+tested independently of response chronology. Legacy session-only readers still\n+use an `updatedAt` fallback. The launch conflict itself and atomic per-assignment\n+run creation/reuse remain open; removing the conflict alone is not sufficient.\n \n","move_path":null},"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -29,2 +29,11 @@\n \n+Both interfaces now bind the selected Run ID through state, asset preload,\n+live updates and actual generated re-entry links. Exact preset assignment,\n+Unicode answers and Run ID survive hard reload; another run's later background\n+saves cannot steal selection or bypass the selected run's monitor pause.\n+Production/development protected SQLite browsers and headless production pass.\n+The second open run in this focused fixture is repository-seeded, not started\n+through the still-blocked P0 workflow. These shared functional safeguards do not\n+close any full rendered-UI acceptance row or pixel-identity claim.\n+\n The shared backend now permits exact preset-assignment resumption after returning\n@@ -69,3 +78,4 @@\n also reproduced: another unfinished Booklet blocks an otherwise available\n-selection, and current-state selection follows answer-update chronology. The\n+selection. Explicit run-bound reads now avoid answer-update chronology, while\n+historical session-only links retain that fallback. The\n mixed rendering fixture completes one Booklet before starting the other; it\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md\nM /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md\nM /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/README.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1791184949456,"completed_at_ms":1791184949461}}
