L=chrome FIRST_SLICE_STORE=memory UI_SMOKE_SKIP_OFFLINE_APP_SHELL=true UI_SMOKE_STOP_AFTER_STEP=participant-entry-sign-in node scripts/smoke-ui.mjs`. The local build passed at 465.90 kB (warning budget exceeded but below 470 kB error); commit `709f9ba` and Entire checkpoint `01M2A1XZJ2DAEA6XQ8S468JQWR` are historical. [Task 2]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- A Playwright `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` at port 4311 means the built API was not running, not an app regression -> verify `/readyz`, start the API, or use the smoke harness. Partial successful CI jobs do not prove final CI; observed run `34675530370` was still in progress. [Task 2]\n- Full Original parity remains open across starter/player/workspace/results/system-check/admin, themes, and equal-viewport screenshot comparisons. Do not call this committed login slice full parity. [Task 2]\n\n# Task Group: Kodierbox read-only VERA pilot-workspace transfer planning\n  duration_ms: 0.13125\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n1..91\n# tests 91\n# suites 0\n# pass 91\n# fail 0\n# cancelled 0\n# skipped 0\n# todo 0\n# duration_ms 1158.682541\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\nparticipant_variant=rewrite: same assignment/run/answer after real starter return and hard reload\nparticipant_selection=rewrite: owned two-run fixture, scoped live acknowledgement, pause/resume and background-save isolation\n(node:21249) ExperimentalWarning: SQLite is an experimental feature and might change at any time\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\nparticipant_variant=original: same assignment/run/answer after real starter return and hard reload\nparticipant_selection=original: owned two-run fixture, scoped live acknowledgement, pause/resume and background-save isolation\nowned_api=shutdown\nbrowser_sign_in=original/1280:HTTP401\nbrowser_sign_in=original/1280:HTTP200\npresence_browser=original/1280: live, two tabs, real close, visible loss, polling, reconnect, answers intact\npresence_browser=rewrite/390: live, two tabs, real close, visible loss, polling, reconnect, answers intact\nbrowser_sign_in=original/390:HTTP401\nbrowser_sign_in=original/390:HTTP200\npresence_browser=original/390: live, two tabs, real close, visible loss, polling, reconnect, answers intact\npresence_silent_socket=60065ms: real server expiry despite an open SSE socket\n\nApplication bundle generation complete. [15.857 seconds] - 2026-10-05T07:26:31.621Z\n\nOutput location: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/dist/apps/web\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":8292},"formatted_output":"- rollout_summaries/2026-09-07T17-47-44-rcM2-testcenter_rewrite_admin_login_and_participant_presence.md (cwd=/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code, rollout_path=/Users/julian/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T19-47-44-01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-04T18:57:47+00:00, thread_id=01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a, partial; administrator login locally verified, CI unfinished)\n\n### keywords\n\n- original-ui, `?ui=original`, Angular Material 20.2.14, MatButton, MatIconModule, inline-svg, original-participant-login, original-login-theme.scss, smoke-ui.mjs, UI_SMOKE_BROWSER_CHANNEL=chrome, 709f9ba, Entire\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user asks for autonomous work, meaningful commits, and no “weiter?” prompts -> continue bounded finished work independently, but preserve `docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx` unchanged and never push unless separately authorized. [Task 1][Task 2]\n- for an “optional verwendbare, mit der Original-UI identischen Oberfläche” -> retain Rewrite UI and shared backend/session semantics; use explicit reversible interface selection rather than replacing the default. [Task 2]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- Original `GET /reviews/export` derives the person from the authenticated token, uses `ReviewDAO::getReviewsByPerson` and `ReviewCSVFormatter`, and returns HTTP 204/no file when empty. The rewrite has participant Review CRUD but still lacks the separate participant-authenticated CSV endpoint and Starter action. Do not confuse workspace/admin `exports/reviews.csv` with this flow; test arbitrary workspace/session filters cannot expose another participant’s reviews. [Task 1]\n- Original login supports name-first/password fallback, password visibility, back navigation, Caps Lock feedback, focus restoration, and shared participant sign-in. `?ui=original` retains Rewrite UI. Angular Material/CDK `20.2.14` is compatible; bundle-budget-safe icons use inline SVG projected with `matButtonIcon`, not `MatIconModule`. [Task 2]\n- Build with `npm run build:web`; focused smoke is `UI_SMOKE_BROWSER_CHANNEL=chrome FIRST_SLICE_STORE=memory UI_SMOKE_SKIP_OFFLINE_APP_SHELL=true UI_SMOKE_STOP_AFTER_STEP=participant-entry-sign-in node scripts/smoke-ui.mjs`. The local build passed at 465.90 kB (warning budget exceeded but below 470 kB error); commit `709f9ba` and Entire checkpoint `01M2A1XZJ2DAEA6XQ8S468JQWR` are historical. [Task 2]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- A Playwright `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` at port 4311 means the built API was not running, not an app regression -> verify `/readyz`, start the API, or use the smoke harness. Partial successful CI jobs do not prove final CI; observed run `34675530370` was still in progress. [Task 2]\n- Full Original parity remains open across starter/player/workspace/results/system-check/admin, themes, and equal-viewport screenshot comparisons. Do not call this committed login slice full parity. [Task 2]\n\n# Task Group: Kodierbox read-only VERA pilot-workspace transfer planning\n  duration_ms: 0.13125\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n1..91\n# tests 91\n# suites 0\n# pass 91\n# fail 0\n# cancelled 0\n# skipped 0\n# todo 0\n# duration_ms 1158.682541\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\nparticipant_variant=rewrite: same assignment/run/answer after real starter return and hard reload\nparticipant_selection=rewrite: owned two-run fixture, scoped live acknowledgement, pause/resume and background-save isolation\n(node:21249) ExperimentalWarning: SQLite is an experimental feature and might change at any time\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\nparticipant_variant=original: same assignment/run/answer after real starter return and hard reload\nparticipant_selection=original: owned two-run fixture, scoped live acknowledgement, pause/resume and background-save isolation\nowned_api=shutdown\nbrowser_sign_in=original/1280:HTTP401\nbrowser_sign_in=original/1280:HTTP200\npresence_browser=original/1280: live, two tabs, real close, visible loss, polling, reconnect, answers intact\npresence_browser=rewrite/390: live, two tabs, real close, visible loss, polling, reconnect, answers intact\nbrowser_sign_in=original/390:HTTP401\nbrowser_sign_in=original/390:HTTP200\npresence_browser=original/390: live, two tabs, real close, visible loss, polling, reconnect, answers intact\npresence_silent_socket=60065ms: real server expiry despite an open SSE socket\n\nApplication bundle generation complete. [15.857 seconds] - 2026-10-05T07:26:31.621Z\n\nOutput location: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/dist/apps/web\n\n"},"started_at_ms":1791185465772,"completed_at_ms":1791185465772}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T07:31:05.778Z","ordinal":82166,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10af9-31b2-7453-97f8-15811101f9ec","call_id":"call_YzoNRgjsOSfdwwzIaUH1u9MM","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"1cdf20\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000021083,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"ecc2b6\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.509150083,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":760,\"output\":\"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\ncde4e227bc7eda7f66f305f5d5573a08fb04357f\\trefs/heads/testcenter-rewrite-parity\\n15c47a80 Bind participant state and live updates to the selected run\\n rewrite-app/README.md                              |  7 +++\\n rewrite-app/apps/api/src/index.ts                  |  9 ++-\\n rewrite-app/apps/api/src/integration.test.ts       | 39 ++++++++++++\\n .../src/app/participant-event-stream.service.ts    | 17 ++++--\\n .../apps/web/src/app/participant-session-links.ts  | 12 ++++\\n .../apps/web/src/app/participant-view.component.ts |  1 +\\n .../apps/web/src/app/participant-view.facade.ts    | 24 +++++---\\n .../apps/web/src/app/runtime-view.facade.ts        | 16 +++--\\n rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md             | 14 ++++-\\n rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md                         | 44 ++++++++++++--\\n rewrite-app/package.json                           |  2 +-\\n rewrite-app/packages/application/src/index.ts      | 26 +++++++-\\n rewrite-app/scripts/event-stream-watchdog.test.mjs | 50 +++++++++++++++-\\n .../scripts/participant-session-links.test.mjs     | 53 +++++++++++++++++\\n .../scripts/smoke-participant-booklet-variant.mjs  | 69 +++++++++++++++++++++-\\n rewrite-app/scripts/smoke-ui.mjs                   |  7 ++-\\n 16 files changed, 354 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)\\nAttach an existing agent session that wasn't captured by hooks.\\n\\nThis creates a checkpoint from the session's transcript and links it to the\\nlast commit. Use this when hooks failed to fire or weren't installed when\\nthe session started, or to attach a research session.\\n\\nIf the last commit already has a checkpoint, the session is added to it.\\nOtherwise a new checkpoint is created.\\n\\nUse --review to tag the attached session as an agent review. The\\nfirst user prompt in the transcript is recorded as the review prompt.\\nPass --skills to declare which skills were actually run; omit to\\nattach a review without a declared skills list.\\n\\nWorks with any registered agent, including external agents enabled via\\nexternal_agents in settings. Run 'entire agent list' to see the full list.\\n\\nIf --agent doesn't locate a transcript, Entire auto-detects the agent from\\nthe transcript and prints the detected agent name.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  entire session attach <session-id> [flags]\\n\\nFlags:\\n  -a, --agent string     Agent that created the session (see 'entire agent list' for registered agents, including external) (default \\\"claude-code\\\")\\n  -f, --force            Skip confirmation and amend the last commit with the checkpoint trailer (best-effort; if the amend fails the checkpoint is still created and the trailer is printed for manual paste)\\n  -h, --help             help for attach\\n      --review           Tag the attached session as an agent review\\n      --skills strings   Optional: declare which review skills were run in this session. Only used with --review\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"a38eef\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008292,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1164,\"output\":\"- rollout_summaries/2026-09-07T17-47-44-rcM2-testcenter_rewrite_admin_login_and_participant_presence.md (cwd=/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code, rollout_path=/Users/julian/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T19-47-44-01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-04T18:57:47+00:00, thread_id=01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a, partial; administrator login locally verified, CI unfinished)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- original-ui, `?ui=original`, Angular Material 20.2.14, MatButton, MatIconModule, inline-svg, original-participant-login, original-login-theme.scss, smoke-ui.mjs, UI_SMOKE_BROWSER_CHANNEL=chrome, 709f9ba, Entire\\n\\n## User preferences\\n\\n- when the user asks for autonomous work, meaningful commits, and no “weiter?” prompts -> continue bounded finished work independently, but preserve `docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx` unchanged and never push unless separately authorized. [Task 1][Task 2]\\n- for an “optional verwendbare, mit der Original-UI identischen Oberfläche” -> retain Rewrite UI and shared backend/session semantics; use explicit reversible interface selection rather than replacing the default. [Task 2]\\n\\n## Reusable knowledge\\n\\n- Original `GET /reviews/export` derives the person from the authenticated token, uses `ReviewDAO::getReviewsByPerson` and `ReviewCSVFormatter`, and returns HTTP 204/no file when empty. The rewrite has participant Review CRUD but still lacks the separate participant-authenticated CSV endpoint and Starter action. Do not confuse workspace/admin `exports/reviews.csv` with this flow; test arbitrary workspace/session filters cannot expose another participant’s reviews. [Task 1]\\n- Original login supports name-first/password fallback, password visibility, back navigation, Caps Lock feedback, focus restoration, and shared participant sign-in. `?ui=original` retains Rewrite UI. Angular Material/CDK `20.2.14` is compatible; bundle-budget-safe icons use inline SVG projected with `matButtonIcon`, not `MatIconModule`. [Task 2]\\n- Build with `npm run build:web`; focused smoke is `UI_SMOKE_BROWSER_CHANNEL=chrome FIRST_SLICE_STORE=memory UI_SMOKE_SKIP_OFFLINE_APP_SHELL=true UI_SMOKE_STOP_AFTER_STEP=participant-entry-sign-in node scripts/smoke-ui.mjs`. The local build passed at 465.90 kB (warning budget exceeded but below 470 kB error); commit `709f9ba` and Entire checkpoint `01M2A1XZJ2DAEA6XQ8S468JQWR` are historical. [Task 2]\\n\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\n\\n- A Playwright `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` at port 4311 means the built API was not running, not an app regression -> verify `/readyz`, start the API, or use the smoke harness. Partial successful CI jobs do not prove final CI; observed run `34675530370` was still in progress. [Task 2]\\n- Full Original parity remains open across starter/player/workspace/results/system-check/admin, themes, and equal-viewport screenshot comparisons. Do not call this committed login slice full parity. [Task 2]\\n\\n# Task Group: Kodierbox read-only VERA pilot-workspace transfer planning\\n  duration_ms: 0.13125\\n  type: 'test'\\n  ...\\n1..91\\n# tests 91\\n# suites 0\\n# pass 91\\n# fail 0\\n# cancelled 0\\n# skipped 0\\n# todo 0\\n# duration_ms 1158.682541\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\nparticipant_variant=rewrite: same assignment/run/answer after real starter return and hard reload\\nparticipant_selection=rewrite: owned two-run fixture, scoped live acknowledgement, pause/resume and background-save isolation\\n(node:21249) ExperimentalWarning: SQLite is an experimental feature and might change at any time\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\nparticipant_variant=original: same assignment/run/answer after real starter return and hard reload\\nparticipant_selection=original: owned two-run fixture, scoped live acknowledgement, pause/resume and background-save isolation\\nowned_api=shutdown\\nbrowser_sign_in=original/1280:HTTP401\\nbrowser_sign_in=original/1280:HTTP200\\npresence_browser=original/1280: live, two tabs, real close, visible loss, polling, reconnect, answers intact\\npresence_browser=rewrite/390: live, two tabs, real close, visible loss, polling, reconnect, answers intact\\nbrowser_sign_in=original/390:HTTP401\\nbrowser_sign_in=original/390:HTTP200\\npresence_browser=original/390: live, two tabs, real close, visible loss, polling, reconnect, answers intact\\npresence_silent_socket=60065ms: real server expiry despite an open SSE socket\\n\\nApplication bundle generation complete. [15.857 seconds] - 2026-10-05T07:26:31.621Z\\n\\nOutput location: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/dist/apps/web\\n\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10af8-f2f3-7321-a574-8ebd6e9ef514","create_time":1791185465.778704}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
